From 011dbe059d202f6f8f28935c98a9cc3373397373 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:05:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_rb_carry_budget_lead, v2_qb_passing_td_k,
 v2_qb_style_blend_k80, v2_keep_fully_excluded_history, v2_points_scale_v6,
 v2_channel_matchups

- v2_rb_carry_budget_lead: split the carry-budget change by carries^2 so the lead back absorbs most of it. An unshipped modifier of the
  shipped v2_rb_carry_budget.
- v2_qb_passing_td_k: K=15 for QB passing TDs alone. Tested 2026-10-06, INCONCLUSIVE (harness v2 START-QB -0.010 CI spans 0, START-ALL
  -0.002, better in 25 of 60 weeks); QB_PASSING_TD_K stays because the shipped v2_qb_td_blend uses it.
- v2_qb_style_blend_k80: QB pass/rush style shrunk with K=80 dropbacks instead of 10 (offline gain START-QB dRMSE -0.0017 at 80, 5 of 5
  seasons); a candidate from the calibration audit that never ran in the full harness.
- v2_keep_fully_excluded_history: a player whose every game was excluded keeps them. Missed its harness bar (START-ALL +0.002 vs
  +0.001; veterans whose only game was cut short lost their prior-season line); the revision v2_keep_fully_excluded_no_prior shipped.
- v2_points_scale_v6: a whole points-scale re-fit (lines, buckets, low end, anchor s). The fit table was never filled: nothing beat the
  shipped scale held out.
- v2_channel_matchups: a name with no gating code (never built; removed from DEFAULT 2026-10-24, measured exactly 0.000).
Removes the lead-weighted option of apply_rb_carry_budget, the K=80 candidate constant, the plain keep-excluded branch, POINTS_SCALE_V6
and its branch in points_scale, and the tests of the removed behavior. Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
